## Rule 45 — Frontend Playwright on cursorMerged [CRITICAL]

- **Author:** **`playwright-frontend`** — `.cursor/skills/playwright-frontend/SKILL.md`, `.cursor/agents/playwright-frontend.md`, command **`.cursor/commands/playwright-frontend.md`**
- **Assessor (once):** **`playwright-frontend-validator`** — `.cursor/skills/playwright-frontend-validator/SKILL.md`. One critique. The author applies it and does not call the assessor again.
- **Branch:** EnergoTS HEAD must already be **`cursorMerged`**. Do not checkout or switch. `cursor` and `staging` are not valid for this rule.
- **Inputs:** `test_cases/Frontend/<Topic>.md` and `test_cases/Frontend/<Topic>.playwright.md` from test-case-generator when the user chose Backend+Frontend.
- **UI evidence:** read-only git on `Cursor-Project/Phoenix/phoenix-ui` (no checkout). Missing locators are recorded with `playwright-cli`, then the existing page object is updated, then specs are written.
- **Spec shape:** `EnergoTS/src/frontend/meterCreate.spec.ts` — API preconditions in `test.step`, `Responses` for JSON, `FrontendResponses` for the on-screen name, then the page object.
- **After the one fix pass:** run `--project=frontend` and report pass, fail, product code defect, and automation defect.
- API specs under `src/tests/` stay with **energo-ts-test** / **playwright-test-validator** / **energo-ts-run**.

Violation is a **BLOCK** when this workflow checkouts EnergoTS or skips the single validator pass before execution.

